{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X_\\eta$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0003": "$\\eta$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$X_\\eta$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$X_\\eta$", "MATH_0008": "$X_\\eta$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:126181b76a68527966f0bec966616f5a20291135857c98afbb591b842d234a97", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f78c1bcb0a776228d7d54a92b13e4f370e899a693861dbd3cf1c27b2390ca64c", "source_text": "Condition (1) implies there are no specializations among the points\nof the fibre <MATH_0001>. Hence (2) holds by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0002> (3) is immediate.\nSince <MATH_0003> is a generic point of <MATH_0004>, the generic points of <MATH_0005>\nare generic points of <MATH_0006>. Hence (3) and \nLemma <REF_0002>\nimply the generic points of <MATH_0007> are also closed.\nThus all points of <MATH_0008> are generic and we see that (1) holds.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0413ea6535411d677dc5e1b9e4b1f4f5ec769ccb08ba6dbd6731d76100eba4bc", "unit_id": "tag:0BAH:proof"}
